&Q000401

{A.1 = 1-8}
11=1.	@wDN{Enlil}, the eminent one, the sovereign lord, whose utterance is trustworthy; @wDN{Nunamnir}, the eternal shepherd of the Land, who hails from the great mountain; the great counsellor, the first and foremost in heaven and on earth, who is in control of all the divine powers; lord, who is imbued with great fearsomeness in accordance with his nobility, a perfected heavenly star, who takes good care of the primeval and choice divine powers, who alone is the lofty god; lord, life-giving light, who leads the people all over the world along one track; huge net spread over heaven and earth, rope stretched over all the lands! Who ever instructed @wDN{Enlil}, who ever rivalled him? 

{A.9 = 9-14}
43=9.	He thought up something of great importance and he made public what his heart, a mighty river, 
47=10.	carried: the hidden secrets (?) of his holy thought. 
52=11.	The matter is a holy and pure one, it concerns the divine powers of the @wTN{E-kur}, 
56=12.	the fated good brick embedded (?) in the bottom of the @fsux{abzu}, it is something most important: 
60=13.	a trustworthy man will rebuild the @wTN{E-kur}, thereby acquiring a lasting name. 
64=14.	The son of this trustworthy man will long hold the sceptre, and their throne will never be overthrown. 

{A.15 = 15-20}
68=15.	To that end, @wDN{Ašimbabbar} appeared shining in the @wTN{E-kur}, pleaded to his father @wDN{Enlil} and made him bring a childbearing mother (?); 
72=16.	in the @wTN{E-duga}, @wDN{Nanna}, the princely son, asked for the thing to happen. 
76=17.	The @fsux{en} priestess gave birth to the trustworthy man from his semen placed in the womb. 
80=18.	@wDN{Enlil}, the powerful shepherd, caused a young man to emerge: a royal child, 
84=19.	one who is perfectly fitted for the throne-dais, 
88=20.	@wRN{Šulgi} the king. 

{A.21 = 21-27}
92=21.	@wDN{Enlil} gave him a good name: 'A lion's seed, who provides the @wTN{E-kur} generously, 
96=22.	the beloved one of @wDN{Ninlil}; the one granted authority in the @wTN{E-kur}; the king of @wSN{Urim}, 
100=23.	the one with shining heart, the shepherd, the protective genius of the Land'. 
104=24.	@wDN{Enlil} chose @wRN{Šulgi} in his pure heart and entrusted the Land to him. 
108=25.	As the shepherd of all the countries, @wDN{Enlil} leant the crook and the staff against his arm, 
112=26.	and placed the immutable sceptre of @wDN{Nanna} in his hand; he made him raise his head high, 
116=27.	sitting on an unshakeable royal seat. 

{A.28 = 28-30}
120=28.	The day was for prayers, the night was for supplications; the Land rested in peace. 
124=29.	The shepherd of prosperity, @wRN{Šulgi}, he with a lasting name, the king of jubilation, 
128=30.	the mighty one, the semen engendered by the faithful man, praised @wDN{Enlil}. 

{A.31 = 31}
134=31.	This is the @fsux{sa-gida}. 

