144=32.	@wRN{Šulgi}, the mighty king, ……, who exults in his triumph, 
148=33.	the …… king vanquished the rebellious land with the @fsux{agakar} weapon of @wDN{Inana}. 

{B.34 = 34}
154=34.	It is the @fsux{ŋišgiŋal} of the @fsux{sa-gida}. 

{C.35 = 35-43}
164=35.	May @wDN{Enlil} the trustworthy, 
168=36.	whose words are lofty -- good fate determined by him takes precedence -- who makes sturdy flax and barley grow -- may he prolong the life of @wRN{Šulgi}, 
172=37.	the provider of the @wTN{E-kur} -- hence its flax is indeed fine flax, 
176=38.	its barley is indeed fine barley -- the property of @wDN{Nanna}, 
180=39.	the houseborn-slave of the @wTN{E-kur}, 
184=40.	him whom @wDN{Ninlil} named at his birth @wRN{Šulgi}, 
188=41.	the shepherd of the Land, 
192=42.	the man whom @wDN{Enlil} knows, 
196=43.	the steward of the temple. 

{C.44 = 44-48}
200=44.	So that its voluminous offering meals would bring joy to the @wTN{E-kur}, 
204=45.	@wDN{Enlil} called upon @wSN{Urim}, the good city founded by the princely one, 
208=46.	the inside of which is a holy treasure chest which, like the @fsux{abzu}, 
212=47.	no eye can see -- the city of good purification rites and pure hand-washing rites; 
216=48.	and what he says is trustworthy. 

{C.49 = 49-53}
220=49.	For his setting up the abundant sacrificial tin cups, 
224=50.	for his having served evening meals in the dining-hall of the @wTN{E-kur}, 
228=51.	@wDN{Enlil} determined a princely fate for the shepherd, 
232=52.	him who is worthy of the kingship and the lofty throne-dais, 
236=53.	@wRN{Šulgi}, who is adorned with the @fsux{ba} garment of the @fsux{en} priests. 

{C.54 = 54-59}
240=54.	The one beautiful like heaven, ……, 
244=55.	@wDN{Nanna}, the king, 
248=56.	the ……, gave him good …… in the @wTN{Ki-ur}, 
252=57.	the great place. At the command (?) of @wDN{Enlil}, 
256=58.	he ……, he roars for him (?) against the foreign land that no one dare oppose. 
260=59.	He stabilizes the countryside, and the people lie at his feet. 

{C.60 = 60-62}
264=60.	@wRN{Šulgi}, the shepherd is the honey man beloved by @wSN{Nibru}; may the true shepherd, @wDN{Šulgi}, refresh himself in the pleasant shade of @wDN{Enlil's} brickwork! 

